# Nous Pilot Codex handoff

## Project

Nous Pilot is a separate development-control-plane project built around the durable Nous Loop. It is intended to make software development agentic from research through implementation, verification, review, repair, and CI/PR follow-up.

## Repository map

- `docs/product/`: user problem, goals, scope, requirements, terminology
- `docs/design/architecture/`: system boundaries and runtime model
- `docs/design/features/`: vertical slices and user-visible workflows
- `docs/design/contracts/`: task, Agent, provider, verification, and integration contracts
- `docs/design/cross-cutting/`: security, policy, observability, and human gates
- `docs/design/decisions/`: architecture decision records
- `docs/operations/`: setup and operational runbooks
- `docs/plans/`: implementation order, checkpoints, and progress
- `src/`: Phase 1 Pilot package, including intake, context, runtime adapter, control plane, orchestration, workspace, and verification
- `tests/`: Phase 1 contract, integration, failure-path, and safety tests
- `examples/`: safe configuration and provider examples

## Design sources of truth

- Product: `docs/product/`
- Architecture: `docs/design/architecture/`
- Features: `docs/design/features/`
- Contracts: `docs/design/contracts/`
- Cross-cutting: `docs/design/cross-cutting/`
- Decisions: `docs/design/decisions/`
- Operations: `docs/operations/`
- Progress: `docs/plans/`

## Core requirement

Nous Pilot must use subagents as a first-class execution boundary. The Coordinator coordinates and judges; it must not silently become the sole planner, implementer, tester, and reviewer.

## Implementation status and next entry point

Phase 1–4 are complete as a local, policy-safe implementation. The normal
user-facing configuration is the single `nous-pilot.toml`; `.nous/config.json`
is generated runtime state. Read [docs/plans/bootstrap-plan.md](./docs/plans/bootstrap-plan.md)
for the implementation plan. Further work should use the existing
[`agent-nous`](../agent-nous/skill/nous/SKILL.md) runtime for hardening or for
separately approved live/remote adapters.

## Constraints

- No secret values in repository artifacts or logs.
- No default live network, paid provider, remote push, merge, or deployment side effects.
- No automatic solo fallback when required subagents are unavailable.
- No hidden holdout prompts or answers in the public repository.
- The external Agent bridge requires an explicit JSON stdin/stdout command; an empty command is a durable blocked state.
- Local apply is human-gated and commit-candidate generation never commits or pushes.
